7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Error
function createError(error, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the error against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the misconception reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the method reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. If the learning record reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 6. Generate an error ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, date_observed now, student_id from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 7. Insert the error record.

Step 8. Insert the error relations.

Step 9. Insert the misconception link, the method link, and the learning link if present.

Step 10. Insert the provenance.

Step 11. Insert the moderation record.

Step 12. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 13. Return the error_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Error
function readError(errorId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the error. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the error relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Error
function updateError(errorId, error, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing error. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new error.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the error_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Error
function deleteError(errorId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing error. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the error_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Query Errors
function queryErrors(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Read the matching errors.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the errors, the count, and the pagination.

7.6 Aggregate Errors
function aggregateErrors(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the aggregation.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the results.

7.7 Full-Text Search
function fullTextSearch(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the search.

Step 3. Read the matching errors.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the errors and the count.

7.8 Export Error
function exportError(errorId, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the deposit.

Step 3. If json, output the deposit. If provo, export to PROV-O. If turtle, serialize to Turtle.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the format.

7.9 Bulk Import
function bulkImport(file, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Parse the file.

Step 3. For each error, call createError.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the results and the count.

7.10 Bulk Export
function bulkExport(query, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the matching errors.

Step 3. If json, output the list. If jsonl, output one line per error. If provo, export each one.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the count.

7.11 Moderate Error
function moderateError(errorId, moderationStatus, moderationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing error. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Update the moderation status. Insert a moderation record.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the error_id and the status.

7.12 Error Map
function errorMap(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all errors.

Step 3. Build the map with subjects as axes and error types as colours.

Step 4. Return the map.

7.13 Error Frequency Curve
function errorFrequencyCurve(studentId, errorId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the error records for the student and the error.

Step 3. Build the curve with the frequency over time.

Step 4. Return the curve.

7.14 Intervention Comparison View
function interventionComparisonView(errorId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the error. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the interventions that have been tried.

Step 4. Build the comparison by overlaying the outcomes.

Step 5. Return the comparison.

7.15 Find Related Errors
function findRelatedErrors(errorId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the error. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Find errors with the same misconception, the same method, the same subject, or the same error type.

Step 4. Return the related errors.

7.16 Audit Log
function auditLog(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Return the results.

7.17 Backup
function backup(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. If sql, dump as SQL. If json, dump as JSON.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the output and the format.

7.18 Restore
function restore(file, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Load the database from the file.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the status restored.

